V4L2 decoder failures fail the decode; three MFC instances (Omarchy Mobile)

Chromium's V4L2StatefulVideoDecoder only logged most device failures: a
CAPTURE queue that could not get its buffers (ApplyResolutionChange() ignored
InitializeCAPTUREQueue()'s result), a failed DQBUF on CAPTURE (polled again
at once) and a failed OUTPUT drain (DecodeCBs never run). On October 8 the
Pixel's MFC ran out of its CMA area during X: decoding went on without frame
buffers until the firmware failed, then s5p-mfc answered POLLIN in its error
state and the GPU work dequeued in a loop for minutes. Now FailDecoding()
runs every pending DecodeCB (and the flush) with kPlatformDecodeFailure,
fails later Decode()s until Reset() and stops watching the device: before
the first frame the pipeline picks the software decoder
(kFallbackAfterDecodeError), after it the player reports a decode error.

GetMaxNumDecoderInstances() returns 3 for s5p-mfc: each H.264 instance keeps
a 2 MiB context in the 8 MiB block that holds the 1 MiB firmware, and a
fourth instance failed only once decoding began. A fourth video decodes in
software from the start.

